(4620896, 666426, 9111, '<td valign="top">As a breast cancer not yet survivor....I love this photo.  There are a few things I''d change, though.  I would have brought her chin a little forward and maybe supported her head in a way to avoid the pushing out of the skin on her right side of her face and putting her head  more inline with her body.  I would have tried this with an open eye too looking at the rose, or even the camera with a gentle look in her eyes.  I''d also put a reflector to the left of the picture to lighten up the shadow under her chin and behind the flower.<br/> <br/>I''m aware that this is will be voted low by people who will look at it in discomfort instead of with happiness that she is a survivor!  If I could vote i''d give it a 7 for the reason mentioned above.</td>', 'As a breast cancer not yet survivor....I love this photo.  There are a few things I''d change, though.  I would have brought her chin a little forward and maybe supported her head in a way to avoid the pushing out of the skin on her right side of her face and putting her head  more inline with her body.  I would have tried this with an open eye too looking at the rose, or even the camera with a gentle look in her eyes.  I''d also put a reflector to the left of the picture to lighten up the shadow under her chin and behind the flower. I''m aware that this is will be voted low by people who will look at it in discomfort instead of with happiness that she is a survivor!  If I could vote i''d give it a 7 for the reason mentioned above.', '2008-04-07 12:45:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(4620899, 666303, 2764, '<td valign="top">Damn - I hate it when I come to a picture that needs to get a 20 and all I can give is a 10 - maybe I can vote twice?  Wow - no more words.</td>', 'Damn - I hate it when I come to a picture that needs to get a 20 and all I can give is a 10 - maybe I can vote twice?  Wow - no more words.', '2008-04-07 12:46:36.000000', NULL, 1),
