(4638569, 666399, 66384, '<td valign="top">I see a long life and one child ;) The halo is distracting for me. Often when I use a strong gausian blur on a background, I  go around the outer edge of the subject with the clone tool.</td>', 'I see a long life and one child ;) The halo is distracting for me. Often when I use a strong gausian blur on a background, I  go around the outer edge of the subject with the clone tool.', '2008-04-14 12:23:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(4638573, 666483, 52115, '<td valign="top">What a serendipitous find!<br/>I''m glad I was able to lend you a <b><i>"Hand"</i></b>. Oil spill was your idea, adding hand was mine.<br/> <br/>No ideas, just go shooting in some direction. Ideas can come up along the way. Joey Lawrence and many others have done that. <b>The "Just do it" attitude.</b> <br/> <br/>To the contrary Tate, we all have changed much, for the better. Congratulations, well deserved.<br/></td>', 'What a serendipitous find!I''m glad I was able to lend you a "Hand". Oil spill was your idea, adding hand was mine. No ideas, just go shooting in some direction. Ideas can come up along the way. Joey Lawrence and many others have done that. The "Just do it" attitude.  To the contrary Tate, we all have changed much, for the better. Congratulations, well deserved.', '2008-04-14 12:30:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(4638593, 666419, 92194, '<td valign="top">I actually like yours better than the one you were inspired by. I like the singularity more.</td>', 'I actually like yours better than the one you were inspired by. I like the singularity more.', '2008-04-14 12:40:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(4638605, 666540, 62318, '<td valign="top">Very cool. That fountain always seems to have good pic opportunities. Perfect fit for the challenge, and I shot I would have been happy to take myself.</td>', 'Very cool. That fountain always seems to have good pic opportunities. Perfect fit for the challenge, and I shot I would have been happy to take myself.', '2008-04-14 12:52:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(4638606, 665836, 31535, '<td valign="top">I figured this might be yours as the processing looks similar to many of your other photos.<br/> <br/>I have to say your shots are unlike any other photog''s on this site. I''m not sure if it''s the PP or a combination of PP/lighting but you''ve created a unique look. The colours blend great but pop in all the right spots. The images are also sharp yet smooth at the same time. Whatever it is, keep up the good work. I enjoy looking.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-04-14 13:51:34.</i></td>', 'I figured this might be yours as the processing looks similar to many of your other photos. I have to say your shots are unlike any other photog''s on this site. I''m not sure if it''s the PP or a combination of PP/lighting but you''ve created a unique look. The colours blend great but pop in all the right spots. The images are also sharp yet smooth at the same time. Whatever it is, keep up the good work. I enjoy looking.', '2008-04-14 12:52:58.000000', '2008-04-14 14:51:34.000000', 0),
(4638609, 666101, 24454, '<td valign="top">Well, it should have indeed scored better than 5.1 in my opinion.  You can so tell that is the calf of a very athletic person. . .kudos to you for staying in such great shape.   I think the photo is very good!!!   The detail is amazing.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Well, it should have indeed scored better than 5.1 in my opinion.  You can so tell that is the calf of a very athletic person. . .kudos to you for staying in such great shape.   I think the photo is very good!!!   The detail is amazing. ', '2008-04-14 12:53:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(4638614, 666419, 92411, '<td valign="top">I would''ve like it a little more blown out on the skin, but its amazing... and I really don''t like nudes... tastefully done indeed!</td>', 'I would''ve like it a little more blown out on the skin, but its amazing... and I really don''t like nudes... tastefully done indeed!', '2008-04-14 12:56:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(4638616, 666183, 24454, '<td valign="top">We had a very similar idea when this challenge came up didn''t we!  Only mine was centered around a baby''s hand and yours was friendship.  I think this is really good, and I agree that the ring adds interest to the photo.  It looks raw and real.  Great job as always, MAK!  I love it when you get higher than you think you are going to get :)<br/> <br/></td>', 'We had a very similar idea when this challenge came up didn''t we!  Only mine was centered around a baby''s hand and yours was friendship.  I think this is really good, and I agree that the ring adds interest to the photo.  It looks raw and real.  Great job as always, MAK!  I love it when you get higher than you think you are going to get :) ', '2008-04-14 12:57:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(4638623, 666419, 24454, '<td valign="top">Wow! Welcome back!  And kudos for breaking the norm and turning out a photo so spectacular that all the typical trends and biases were kicked out the window.  A high key nude submitted in a non-nude challenge -- and blue ribboning!   THAT is quite something! <br/> <br/>CONGRATULATIONS on all of it!  The photo is breathtaking!<br/> <br/></td>', 'Wow! Welcome back!  And kudos for breaking the norm and turning out a photo so spectacular that all the typical trends and biases were kicked out the window.  A high key nude submitted in a non-nude challenge -- and blue ribboning!   THAT is quite something!  CONGRATULATIONS on all of it!  The photo is breathtaking! ', '2008-04-14 13:02:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(4638651, 665559, 33769, '<td valign="top">this was one of the great shots -  the drop of milk -does- resemble a tear splashing down on the palm, i am really surprised this didn''t finish higher up - its an interesting effect you created witht eh milk in the palm -and its in focus beautifully-<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-04-14 12:13:22.</i></td>', 'this was one of the great shots -  the drop of milk -does- resemble a tear splashing down on the palm, i am really surprised this didn''t finish higher up - its an interesting effect you created witht eh milk in the palm -and its in focus beautifully-', '2008-04-14 13:12:53.000000', '2008-04-14 13:13:22.000000', 0),
(4638656, 666321, 68586, '<td valign="top">Didn''t vote in this as I have been off having a good time - but 154th !! LOL<br/> <br/>Don''t stop the challenges Deb - keep them comming  :- )<br/> <br/></td>', 'Didn''t vote in this as I have been off having a good time - but 154th !! LOL Don''t stop the challenges Deb - keep them comming  :- ) ', '2008-04-14 13:18:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(4638665, 666516, 89723, '<td valign="top">Thank you for all of your comments!! The main reason I joined this website was to improve on my photography skills and share ideas with other like minded individuals. As I read each of your comments over the week, I decided I would implement some of the suggestions to see how they work. <br/> <br/>Here they are:<br/> <br/><img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=9462" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">kali</a> and <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=61651" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">krnodil</a> requested a portrait orientation.<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=669301" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/85000-89999/89723/120/669301.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/85000-89999/89723/120/669301.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/85000-89999/89723/120/669301.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/><img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=59415" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">jason_cross</a> requested I fix the head alignment and see it in black and white.<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=669299" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/85000-89999/89723/120/669299.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/85000-89999/89723/120/669299.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/85000-89999/89723/120/669299.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/><img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/31.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/31.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/31.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=78196" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">figaro</a> requested a fade on the feet. <br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=669300" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/85000-89999/89723/120/669300.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/85000-89999/89723/120/669300.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/85000-89999/89723/120/669300.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>Other comments that I couldn''t accommodate at this time were adding hands and using a different DOF on the feet. I really wish I would have used hands as well. I may re-shoot this with hands for my personal use. <br/> <br/>By the way, I really like the way the portrait version looks. Can we do this challenge over? :)<br/> <br/>Here is the original:<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=669357" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/85000-89999/89723/120/669357.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/85000-89999/89723/120/669357.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/85000-89999/89723/120/669357.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>Thanks again.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-04-14 16:06:00.</i></td>', 'Thank you for all of your comments!! The main reason I joined this website was to improve on my photography skills and share ideas with other like minded individuals. As I read each of your comments over the week, I decided I would implement some of the suggestions to see how they work.  Here they are:  kali and  krnodil requested a portrait orientation.    jason_cross requested I fix the head alignment and see it in black and white.    figaro requested a fade on the feet.    Other comments that I couldn''t accommodate at this time were adding hands and using a different DOF on the feet. I really wish I would have used hands as well. I may re-shoot this with hands for my personal use.  By the way, I really like the way the portrait version looks. Can we do this challenge over? :) Here is the original:   Thanks again.', '2008-04-14 13:26:08.000000', '2008-04-14 17:06:00.000000', 0),
(4638677, 665559, 69325, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by redpanda:</b></div><hr/><i> I don''t really get it... Those don''t look like tears (unless from seriously infected eyes). </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>you never heard the old expression "don''t cry over spilled milk"?<br/> <br/>awesome shot by the way</td>', 'Originally posted by redpanda: I don''t really get it... Those don''t look like tears (unless from seriously infected eyes).   you never heard the old expression "don''t cry over spilled milk"? awesome shot by the way', '2008-04-14 13:41:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(4638721, 666483, 68504, '<td valign="top">(Haven''t had time to look at much lately, and when I saw the thumbnail, no title, I thought How did they get so small a hand on the eye of a peacock feather?)  The photo challenges the mind to catch up with the message: at once we extract the oil and waste its rainbow fallout and with the same hand reach for and crave ever more.  Our grimy/oil stained hand.<br/>How delightful this was a sort of collaboration.</td>', '(Haven''t had time to look at much lately, and when I saw the thumbnail, no title, I thought How did they get so small a hand on the eye of a peacock feather?)  The photo challenges the mind to catch up with the message: at once we extract the oil and waste its rainbow fallout and with the same hand reach for and crave ever more.  Our grimy/oil stained hand.How delightful this was a sort of collaboration.', '2008-04-14 14:13:33.000000', NULL, 0),
