(4643637, 665416, 52614, '<td valign="top">This really caught my attention... and then to find out it was a self-portrait; well, I do know how difficult they can be!<br/> <br/>The composition is nice, the red-red lips reach down to a visceral/animal part of me (''perfect'' is what pops into my mind), and the quirky expression makes it just right. If I looked as good as you, maybe I''d try this myself! ;)</td>', 'This really caught my attention... and then to find out it was a self-portrait; well, I do know how difficult they can be! The composition is nice, the red-red lips reach down to a visceral/animal part of me (''perfect'' is what pops into my mind), and the quirky expression makes it just right. If I looked as good as you, maybe I''d try this myself! ;)', '2008-04-16 12:07:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(4643653, 666532, 59194, '<td valign="top">I agree with most of the comments - I would like to have seen the hand a bit more in focus.  I like the contrast of the lower part of the photo and would even consider cropping it half way up the thumb.  The top of the photo doesn''t add much in my opinion.  Just my 2cents.</td>', 'I agree with most of the comments - I would like to have seen the hand a bit more in focus.  I like the contrast of the lower part of the photo and would even consider cropping it half way up the thumb.  The top of the photo doesn''t add much in my opinion.  Just my 2cents.', '2008-04-16 12:16:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(4643681, 666419, 78062, '<td valign="top">Larus,<br/> <br/>since you asked, the person who originally did this shot was Sascha Huettenhain, a German photographer specializing in erotic fine art. There are a few differences between hers and yours- she has a higher position of the legs so they touch the chin and i think it''s a square crop also. On hers, the way the limbs are positioned makes a weird geometric effect as you can''t see any of the joints... it''s actually really neat the more you look at it, the cooler it gets.<br/> <br/>I think the picture might be called "Lena" but don''t quote me on that one... i had a look around and there''s a fair few emulations of it doing the rounds.<br/> <br/>Congrats on your ribbon btw- this isn''t about that, but rather filling you in since you asked for some info. Hope it helps :)</td>', 'Larus, since you asked, the person who originally did this shot was Sascha Huettenhain, a German photographer specializing in erotic fine art. There are a few differences between hers and yours- she has a higher position of the legs so they touch the chin and i think it''s a square crop also. On hers, the way the limbs are positioned makes a weird geometric effect as you can''t see any of the joints... it''s actually really neat the more you look at it, the cooler it gets. I think the picture might be called "Lena" but don''t quote me on that one... i had a look around and there''s a fair few emulations of it doing the rounds. Congrats on your ribbon btw- this isn''t about that, but rather filling you in since you asked for some info. Hope it helps :)', '2008-04-16 12:30:07.000000', NULL, 0),
